{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# LLM provider seam — first-class Bedrock + best-effort OpenAI-compatible, with tiered verdict provenance\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nrebar's LLM runtime is provider-agnostic in principle but Anthropic-shaped in practice. `runner.py:268`\nbranches on `resolved.startswith(\"anthropic\")` to build the retrying transport; `runner.py:316` gates prompt\ncaching on the same string; `structured.py:46` picks the output mode from a hardcoded\n`_NATIVE_OUTPUT_PROVIDERS` name set; and `runner.py:653` (`_pai_check_config`) REFUSES `base_url`/`api_key`\noutright. That refusal was deliberate — commit `75e598a41` records it as \"a loud guard that REFUSES\nbase_url/api_key rather than silently dropping them (a capability gap vs langgraph, surfaced not hidden)\" —\nbut `docs/llm-framework.md:126-133,226` already documents `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL`/`REBAR_LLM_API_KEY` as working,\nand `config.py:502-503,611-612` already parses them. The documentation is currently false.\n\nMeanwhile our clients will reach Claude through **AWS Bedrock more often than through the direct Anthropic\nAPI**, and rebar has no Bedrock path at all. GitHub PR #120/#121 surfaced this: #121 proposed fronting Bedrock\nwith an OpenAI-compatible gateway, which works but silently gives up prompt caching, the retrying tenacity\ntransport, the per-request read timeout, and native structured output — and records a `model` string in the\nSIGNED verdict sidecar (`plan_review/sidecar.py:601`, `completion_sidecar.py:206`) that no longer names what\nactually answered.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdopt pydantic-ai's own extension points instead of inventing rebar-specific ones.\n\n1. **Seam = `provider_factory`.** pydantic-ai's `infer_model()` accepts a `provider_factory` hook; upstream\n   issue pydantic-ai#1343 explicitly directs user-configurable-provider apps to it rather than patching\n   `infer_provider`. rebar keeps `provider:model` strings as the single selector (already the design in\n   `anthropic_model.py:159` `_pai_model`) and supplies ONE factory that returns configured `Provider` objects.\n   The inline anthropic branch at `runner.py:268` becomes a factory entry, not a special case.\n2. **Capabilities = `ModelProfile`.** pydantic-ai exposes a per-vendor capability profile at `model.profile`.\n   Output-mode selection and cache settings read the profile instead of matching provider name strings.\n   Bedrock-hosted Anthropic gets a rebar `ModelProfile` override, which is the documented upstream guidance\n   precisely because Bedrock's capability flags differ from the direct Anthropic API.\n3. **Two support tiers.** First-class = Anthropic + Bedrock: native builders, full fidelity, covered by tests\n   and the parity bar. Best-effort = everything else through one OpenAI-compatible builder.\n4. **Provenance carries the tier.** The signed sidecar's `model` field widens to structured provenance\n   (provider, model, endpoint host, tier, effective capabilities) so a consumer can tell a first-class verdict\n   from a best-effort one.\n5. **Dogfood on the review bot.** The AWS-hosted code-review bot cuts over to Claude via Bedrock.\n\n**Alternative rejected: LiteLLM as an in-process SDK** (the aider / OpenHands pattern). It buys 100+ providers\nfor one dependency, but its normalization layer is documented to drift on exactly what rebar depends on —\nprompt-cache semantics, tool-call shapes, and cost accounting — and neither aider nor OpenHands escapes\nper-provider code anyway (OpenHands still carries a `model_features.py` registry and two auto-detected\ncompletion modes). rebar chose pydantic-ai for weight and structured-output reliability; adding LiteLLM\nin-process would duplicate its model layer. A LiteLLM *proxy* remains reachable through the best-effort\nOpenAI-compatible builder, so breadth is preserved without the dependency.\n\n**Alternative rejected: gateway-only Bedrock** (PR #121's approach). It requires every operator to stand up and\naccredit a proxy, and gives up caching, thinking, native structured output, and the retrying transport. The\nnative `BedrockConverseModel` path needs no proxy and supports prompt caching via `BedrockModelSettings`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — replace the inline anthropic branch (`:268`) and the cache gate (`:316`) with\n  factory + profile lookups; retire the `_pai_check_config` refusal (`:653`).\n- `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py` — the anthropic builder moves behind the factory; `_pai_model` (`:159`)\n  stays the string resolver.\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured.py` — `output_mode` (`:51`) reads the profile instead of `_NATIVE_OUTPUT_PROVIDERS`\n  (`:46`).\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — `base_url`/`api_key`/`model_provider` (`:501-503`) composition semantics.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`, `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py` — provenance payload.\n- `src/rebar/llm/parity.py` — the Bedrock-vs-Anthropic parity run.\n- `pyproject.toml` — a `[bedrock]` optional extra.\n- `infra/terraform/main.tf` (`:50-54` `metadata_options`), `infra/terraform/iam.tf`, `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh`.\n- `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/env-vars.md`, a new ADR.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- rebar runs a gate against AWS Bedrock Claude with prompt caching measured as effective (or the measurement\n  recorded as negative with a decision), no gateway required.\n- No module selects provider behavior by matching a provider-name string; provider construction happens in\n  exactly one factory and capability decisions read the model profile.\n- `REBAR_LLM_BASE_URL` works as `docs/llm-framework.md` already claims, composing with\n  `REBAR_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER` per the documented recipe.\n- A signed verdict states which provider, endpoint, and support tier produced it.\n- The production review bot votes `LLM-Review` using Bedrock, with no direct-Anthropic fallback, and an alarm\n  on `VOTER_ERROR`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] every child story is closed and its change is `Verified +1` on Gerrit\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `rebar review-plan` and `rebar verify-completion` both run green against Bedrock in a live env-gated\n      check, evidenced by the run output attached as a comment on the Bedrock story\n- [ ] `grep -rn 'startswith(\"anthropic\")' src/rebar/llm/` returns no provider-selection branch outside the\n      provider factory module\n- [ ] the review bot's most recent `LLM-Review` vote on a real change carries Bedrock provenance in its sidecar"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785011305524557001,"uuid":"95d538c5-3564-457c-84f7-293f32ff15e9"}